    "long_instructions": "Welcome back! Your web page now has a title. Let's give your pet fish a starring role!\r\n\r\n1. Open the `index.html` file.\r\n2. Find the `<body>` tags. Remember, the `<body>` is where all the visible content of your web page goes.\r\n3. Inside the `<body>` tags, add an `<h1>` tag.\r\n4. Between the opening `<h1>` and closing `</h1>` tags, type the name of your pet fish. For example, if your fish's name is \"Finley\", you would type `<h1>Finley</h1>`.\r\n\r\nThis will make your fish's name appear as the biggest heading on your web page!",
    "generate_outline": "Students will add an `<h1>` tag inside the `<body>` of their HTML document. The content of the `<h1>` tag should be the name of their pet fish, e.g., 'Goldie' or 'Finley'."
